{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/934326-complex-litany-problems","id":934326,"title":"Complex Litany problems","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-20T00:07:31-07:00","id":934326,"title":"Complex Litany problems","content":"I am thinking of creating a blind weak willed Philodox Metis to tag along to a PC pack, so they have some indication if what they do is against the litany. So to impress them i came up with several &quot;scenarios&quot; he can cite like important case to show off his prowess.<br /> Things like the status of &quot;war&quot; is generally declared on sept level and why a pack alpha can not declare it and its implications or who is able to change the litany? What about the Child of Gaia who are not really following &quot;Do Not Suffer Thy People to Tend Thy Sickness&quot;.<br /> <br /> So, what where your most complicated problems that you guys encountered with the Litany? When did you guys felt like lawyers and tried to interpret every word that was written?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash","name":"Crytash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T00:19:11-07:00","id":934329,"title":"","content":"Ive never had it come up that much thankfully, except some people who argued theirs only 2 real rules in there.mostly because they didnt understand that the gift &quot;Sense wyrm&quot; Makes &quot;Wherever it breeds and wherever it dwells&quot; Less subjective then it might otherwise be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T00:37:21-07:00","id":934336,"title":"","content":"As I've played a lot of philodox, a lot.<br /> <br /> Though, these are mostly difficult due to the situations they are tied to. One recent was a case of a very anti-garou cub getting throathed by a Fenrir, with the Den Father saying the Fenrir did not respect those below them in their actions. While the cub in questions was veering close to insanity out of fear. The case was hard not because of the litany really, but more because no matter the philodox did, there would be no good resolution. The Fenrir was justified to make the cub submit, yet the Den Father and cub were devastated. The cub eventually running away to the umbra when they saw no justice to themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T00:50:46-07:00","id":934340,"title":"","content":"Most common problems <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>It is meant to be a compilation of songs and howls and tales, but it is only a list of some one-liners.</li> <li>It is meant to be intuitive, but players, and homid characters, tend to get caught up on the words instead of the meaning.</li> <li>It is meant to be the part of the local laws that are equal to (almost) all septs and tribes, not the only laws there are.</li> </ol><br /> <br /> That said, I would see a lot of Get of Fenris don't give a shit if &quot;war&quot; was declared or not. It depends on the consensus of the society whether or not they are at war. I can see a pack on a mission in a planning phase and in an execution phase of their mission. During one it is okay to challenge the alpha, of suggestions or simply laying out a better play doesn't work, during the latter it is not acceptable. There is no need to declare it. Same goes for septs. There might be some grey area, when the plan is under way, but the fighting hasn't started yet.<br /> <br /> For a Philodox or Galliard, it should be easy to come up with three to five local stories that illustrate each point of the litany. But, since White Wolf didn't provide any, you have to come up with them yourself. That is a lot of work.<br /> <br /> It was I think Genghis Khan who said, that the spirit of a law is important, not the words. Especially with the &quot;mate&quot;, &quot;war&quot;, &quot;sickness&quot; words, the meaning is different to everyone. Still, this are sentences, that try to convey something a lupus can understand in the English language. And how messy this is, you can see if someone tries to translate the Litany into other human languages. The Litany isn't originally in modern English, is it. So, just because you are the biggest guy at the railway terminal, you shouldn't get the first stock the guy your murdered ever bought.<br /> <br /> --------<br /> <br /> <br /> Tend sickness<ul><li>a story could tell of a sept who starved over the winter and was taken over by Get of Fenris, because they spend too much of the resources for their old.</li> <li>another story could tell of a leader who became sick, but was mentally still fit. So he was tended to, and when he died he still hadn't taught his skills to a worthy successor.</li> <li>the most basic aspect would be, that the pack couldn't hunt for the sick one was holding them back.</li> </ul><br /> War Time<ul><li>A story where there was no plan, as the pack/sept was attacked, and while the leaders commands were reckless they would have been sufficient to throw back the attack, but due to the interference of would-be-leaders the whole thing went south.</li> <li>A story where the commands of the leader were seemingly stupid, for he had compartmentalised the information about backup and such. Arguing or even a challenge leads to the window of opportunity to enact the plan closing.</li> <li>A story where a younger challenger was better at combat and beat the leader in a challenge to become the new leader, but lacked the support of neighbouring septs - or started a whole number of subsequent challenges till the danger was at the gates.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> For each story, any good Ragabash should have a story where defying a tenet of the litany actually brought about a good outcome. Just so he can test the conviction of his peers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T02:22:12-07:00","id":934359,"title":"","content":"I think it's excellent plot fodder that the Litany is so open eneded and that there is the whole role of Philodox &amp; Ragabash. It allows for some amazing roleplaying and exploration of the themes behind the Garou society and how they refract our own societies and mores.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T02:44:43-07:00","id":934367,"title":"","content":"True. However, in LARP you usually need preparation to work out what you like to present, so some material to help from White Wolf would have been appreciated....<br /> <br /> &quot;My character steps in front of the crowd and lays down an opposing view, reminding everyone that sometimes new ways are required, as is evident in some old tale, that I recite to make my point. 4 successes on Wits+Performance sure should sway some of the garou to my side of the argument.&quot;<br /> That's just not something that would work in (nordic) LARP. So playing with the theme can run into some grave problems, pretty fast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T03:33:34-07:00","id":934379,"title":"","content":"That would be a really cool book. Something i would be gladly inclined to buy, if it is not too expensive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash","name":"Crytash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T04:02:04-07:00","id":934387,"title":"","content":"Could also be something for a writing challenge. I'd be happy to host such a tale collection...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T06:13:27-07:00","id":934436,"title":"","content":"Agreed on the Litany book. Or, maybe do an updated Silver Record that HAS the full litany in it, plus the tale of the Silver Crown,etc. Because those are things that you would actually need playing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T06:18:56-07:00","id":934440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/934326-complex-litany-problems?p=934367#post934367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True. However, in LARP you usually need preparation to work out what you like to present, so some material to help from White Wolf would have been appreciated....<br /> <br /> &quot;My character steps in front of the crowd and lays down an opposing view, reminding everyone that sometimes new ways are required, as is evident in some old tale, that I recite to make my point. 4 successes on Wits+Performance sure should sway some of the garou to my side of the argument.&quot;<br /> That's just not something that would work in (nordic) LARP. So playing with the theme can run into some grave problems, pretty fast.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect it works waaaay better in Nordic LARP than American LARP. There's a really big attitude of &quot;Don't tell me how to play my character&quot; in American LARPing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T06:33:00-07:00","id":934449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/934326-complex-litany-problems?p=934436#post934436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed on the Litany book. Or, maybe do an updated Silver Record that HAS the full litany in it, plus the tale of the Silver Crown,etc. Because those are things that you would actually need playing.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that was my point, there is no FULL litany.<br /> It is stated, that the tenets were condensed of all the folklore of all the tribes, once their &quot;top dogs&quot; met at Pangea an could actually let go of their tribal natures to find what made them equal as garou. But the tribal and local stories, songs and possibly other forms of art (the Crescent Moon clan has a mountain-side of pictorgrams) still exist and for any local sept, they are still the most relevant factors why the litany is important. And they still have equally high held laws, that are not globally accepted as essential of garou nature and therefore never made it into the litany.<br /> <br /> If, for every tenet of the litany two or three legends exists, just as examples on how such stories could look like, and maybe an handful of shorter ideas for players to orient their own stories at, that would be enough. There is no real need for any book that has the claim to be THE whole epic compilation of all the songs that would take hours to recite. Besides, should it be modern english or more like a tape of wolf howls to be memorized ?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/934326-complex-litany-problems?p=934440#post934440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suspect it works waaaay better in Nordic LARP than American LARP. There's a really big attitude of &quot;Don't tell me how to play my character&quot; in American LARPing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, MET still has rules on how certain traits affect other characters. Damage being the most obvious one. I never played MET, for it is so not popular in Germany.<br /> The way we play here, one would need to actually the tale and no traits will make it appear better, if you screw this up. Then again, you would also need to take a swing at another players torso or arms to deal damage...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T06:52:25-07:00","id":934461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/934326-complex-litany-problems?p=934449#post934449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that was my point, there is no FULL litany.<br /> It is stated, that the tenets were condensed of all the folklore of all the tribes, once their &quot;top dogs&quot; met at Pangea an could actually let go of their tribal natures to find what made them equal as garou. But the tribal and local stories, songs and possibly other forms of art (the Crescent Moon clan has a mountain-side of pictorgrams) still exist and for any local sept, they are still the most relevant factors why the litany is important. And they still have equally high held laws, that are not globally accepted as essential of garou nature and therefore never made it into the litany.<br /> <br /> If, for every tenet of the litany two or three legends exists, just as examples on how such stories could look like, and maybe an handful of shorter ideas for players to orient their own stories at, that would be enough. There is no real need for any book that has the claim to be THE whole epic compilation of all the songs that would take hours to recite. Besides, should it be modern english or more like a tape of wolf howls to be memorized ?.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much this. It would also be cool if each tribe had their own chosen tale, to support how they see the tenet.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}